{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "Which head-tracking repos migrate to the canonical config format, and where each one's",
    "config lives. scripts/check-config-format.mjs (pixi run check-config-format, part of",
    "pixi run check) validates the shape and pins `legacy`.",
    "",
    "`legacy`: every repo that published a pre-canonical build, a v* release or the rolling",
    "dev pre-release on GitHub, keyed by its current name. Only these carry a frozen legacy",
    "import. The set is frozen: the validator pins the SHA-256 of the sorted names, so adding",
    "or removing one fails the check. `predecessors` names earlier repos of the same mod that",
    "published releases, whose shipped files are differential-test inputs; `renamed_from` is",
    "the repo's name before a GitHub rename, which local checkouts may still carry.",
    "",
    "`exempt`: repos that cannot move to a canonical reader, or have no config, with the reason.",
    "A repo in neither `legacy` nor `exempt` must be canonical and carry no legacy import.",
    "",
    "`configs`: each migrating repo's config files. `committed` is the repo path of the rendered",
    "file, null until the conversion commits one where the repo tracks none today. `installed`",
    "is every path the file takes relative to the game folder, one per store layout, empty only",
    "with a `no_installed_reason`, and every one is named CameraUnlock.ini. `legacy_source` is",
    "a bare file name, with no folder: the file the repo's pre-canonical builds read, in the",
    "folder of each installed path, or the folder no_installed_reason names. The mod imports",
    "it once while CameraUnlock.ini is absent and never writes it. It is set exactly for a repo",
    "in `legacy`, and null for every other repo, since no player holds an older file. `dialect` is",
    "native (key names, or 0x hex for a key with no name) or unity (key names only), for the",
    "hotkey lint. unity is also what tells the README config block that the repo's config owner",
    "is core's C# one, the only owner that runs natively on Linux and macOS, so a C# repo is",
    "unity and every other repo native. Game paths use backslashes, as install scripts and",
    "PRESERVE_FILES write them; repo paths use forward slashes, as git writes them.",
    "",
    "`normalisations` and `approved_changes`: the only differences a differential test may",
    "allow between the import and the migration, beside a moved default's no-file input.",
    "`approved` is the date the owner approved one; a normalisation with `approved` null is",
    "pending and no map may apply it. `drop_rule` names the DropRule the import records.",
    "",
    "`conversion_notes`: per repo in `configs`, facts the owner decided that its conversion and",
    "differential test follow: `text` and the `approved` date.",
    "",
    "`allow_legacy_symbols`: per repo, uses of a symbol the legacy-reader check bans that do not",
    "read the mod's config: `symbol` as the check reports it (GetPrivateProfileStringA, IniReader,",
    "ConfigFile.Bind), `file` the repo path and `reason`.",
    "",
    "`per_game`: per repo in `configs`, the global concept rows the game keeps for itself",
    "instead of taking them from Defaults.ini: `row` the concept id, `reason` and the `approved`",
    "date, which every entry needs. The game's table marks each such row PerGame(), and the",
    "committed file holds its value there, where every other global concept row holds default;",
    "the canonical config lint holds the file to that. A concept data/config-schema.json marks",
    "`\"global\": false` (CollisionMargin, CollisionChannel) is never an entry: every game keeps",
    "those already, as Engine rows. A chord a game binds itself is a per_game",
    "hotkey row, whose reason names the chord it replaces and the one it uses. An entry added",
    "after the repo's first converted release changes what default means in files already on",
    "players' disks, since those rows stop following Defaults.ini, so it is a breaking change for",
    "that repo. scripts/check-config-descriptor.mjs requires a launcher-manifest.json config",
    "descriptor's `per_game` to name exactly these rows, each with the value text the committed",
    "file holds there."
  ],
